# Website mockups — repo workflow

This repository is the single place for client website mockups. Do **not** create separate GitHub repos (including under `razzinteractive`) for each project. Develop here and **push to `main`**.

## Stack

- Use regular **HTML**, **CSS**, and **JavaScript** (and common JS libraries when useful).
- Do not introduce React/Next/other app frameworks unless explicitly requested.
- More design and process rules will be added as other projects start.

## New project folder

When starting a project, create a **root-level folder** named after the project (kebab-case), e.g. `kalos/`.

- Put all mockup pages, assets, CSS, and JS **inside that folder**.
- Versioned work for the same client goes inside the project folder (e.g. `kalos/v1/`, `kalos/v2/`).
- Follow established rules and the design guidance for that mockup.

## Project index (summary)

Inside each project folder, include an `index.html` that is the **summary / guide view**:

- Title and short description of the project
- List **all important project links** (version guides, homepage/prototype, PDFs, etc.)
- Links open in a new tab: `target="_blank"` and `rel="noreferrer noopener"`

### Link format example

```html
<a
  href="https://yeraysresman.github.io/kalos/v2/v2.html"
  rel="noreferrer noopener"
  title="https://yeraysresman.github.io/kalos/v2/v2.html"
  target="_blank"
>https://yeraysresman.github.io/kalos/v2/v2.html</a>
```

Prefer live GitHub Pages URLs when they exist; otherwise use relative paths inside the project folder (still with `target="_blank"` and `rel="noreferrer noopener"`).

## Checklist for a new project

1. Create `/<project-name>/` at the repo root
2. Add `/<project-name>/index.html` as the summary with the full link list
3. Build mockups under that folder (HTML/CSS/JS)
4. Push to `main` and keep the summary updated when links change
